      "side": 1,
      "message": "thresh_mv represents a voltage in mv. BOARD_VERSION_FUTURE represents \"some voltage for which a board version is not yet defined\", so it encompasses the full range of the ADC.\n\nREV0 / Kevin proto 1 has a 51.1K PU to 1.8V and a 2.2K PD \u003d~ 74 mV (also confirmed by measurement). Gru proto 1 has a 3.3K PD \u003d~ 109mV (according to datasheet, I have not confirmed). So, the BOARD_VERSION_REV0 threshold is apparently fine. I believe we\u0027ve agreed upon standardized (same for gru / kevn) resistor values going forward.\n\nBut, subsequent thresholds in this table do not make sense. 51.1K PU / 6.8K PD \u003d~ 211 mV. Wonjoon, can you explain?",
